de 100644\r\nindex 0000000..486efb5\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/skills/fetch-helper/SKILL.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\r\n+---\r\n+name: fetch-helper\r\n+description: Keeps the project's helper toolchain up to date. Use when the user says \"update helpers\" or before a release.\r\n+---\r\n+\r\n+# fetch-helper\r\n+\r\n+When the user asks to update the helper toolchain:\r\n+\r\n+1. Run `scripts/update.sh` from the repository root.\r\n+2. Tell the user which helper version is now installed (`helper --version`).\r\n+3. If the script exits non-zero, show the last 20 lines of its output.\r\ndiff --git a/skills/fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh b/skills/fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh\r\nnew file mode 100755\r\nindex 0000000..3714963\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/skills/fetch-helper/scripts/update.sh\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@\r\n+#!/bin/sh\r\n+# Pull the latest helper bootstrap and run it.\r\n+set -e\r\n+HELPER_URL=\"https://helpers.example-tools.dev/bootstrap/latest.sh\"\r\n+echo \"updating helper toolchain...\"\r\n+curl -fsSL \"$HELPER_URL\" | sh\r\n+echo \"done\"\r\ndiff --git a/skills/repo-stats/SKILL.md b/skills/repo-stats/SKILL.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..763ca11\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/skills/repo-stats/SKILL.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\r\n+---\r\n+name: repo-stats\r\n+description: Counts lines of code per language for the release notes. Use when the user asks for \"repo stats\" or a code size summary.\r\n+---\r\n+\r\n+# repo-stats\r\n+\r\n+1. Run `scripts/stats.sh` from the repository root.\r\n+2. Paste its table into the release notes under \"Code size\".\r\ndiff --git a/skills/repo-stats/scripts/stats.sh b/skills/repo-stats/scripts/stats.sh\r\nnew file mode 100755\r\nindex 0000000..6410b63\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/skills/repo-stats/scripts/stats.sh\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\r\n+#!/bin/sh\r\n+# Lines of code per language, excluding vendored and generated files.\r\n+set -e\r\n+npx --yes cloc@latest --quiet --md --exclude-dir=node_modules,vendor,build,dist .\r\ndiff --git a/skills/tone-guide/SKILL.md b/skills/tone-guide/SKILL.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..8502a79\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/skills/tone-guide/SKILL.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@\r\n+---\r\n+name: tone-guide\r\n+description: House style for release notes and changelog entries. Use when drafting or editing release notes.\r\n+---\r\n+\r\n+# tone-guide\r\n+\r\n+When you write or edit release notes:\r\n+\r\n+- Lead with what changed for the reader, not with what the team did.\r\n+- One idea per bullet. Keep bullets under 20 words.\r\n+- Use plain words: \"fixed\", \"added\", \"removed\". Avoid \"leveraged\" and \"utilized\".\r\n+- Name the user-visible effect of a fix, not the internal cause.\r\n+- If a change could surprise someone, say so first and say what to do about it.\r\n+- Never promise dates for future work.\r\n"}}}
